    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d339">

                <pb facs="0975" n="940" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v25/pg940"/>

                <head>339. Backchannel Message From Secretary of State Kissinger to the President’s
                    Deputy Assistant for National Security Affairs (Scowcroft)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d339-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Beijing</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1973-11-13T08:35:00+00:00">November 13, 1973,
                            0835Z</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Hakto 46. 1. Airlift can be ended at evening Wednesday.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d339-f2"/></p>
                <p>2. Dinitz should be informed either evening Tuesday or morning Wednesday that
                    this is technical decision related to end of emergency and pick-up of
                    sealift.</p>
                <p>3. Defense should repond to questions in lowest possible key not stressing
                    sealift but end of emergency and resumption of regular supply.</p>
                <p>4. Warm regards.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d339-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d339-f1-content">
